@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Eve runtime
+
+This project uses the nested `agent/` layout and requires Node.js 24 or newer. Eve supports exact lowercase `instructions.md`, `instructions.ts`, or non-recursive `.md`/`.ts` entries under `instructions/`; it rejects colliding root `instructions.md` and `instructions.ts`. Static tools use `tools/<name>.ts`. Skills may be flat `<name>.md`, packaged `<name>/SKILL.md` with description frontmatter, or `<name>.ts` using `defineSkill`. Local subagents use `subagents/<id>/agent.ts`; the single-file `subagents/<id>.ts` alternative is for `defineRemoteAgent`.
+
+Dynamic resolution must be verified at its lifecycle event. Remote agents, extension contributions, connection-provided and framework tools, filesystem-name collisions, reserved names, and advanced runtime behavior require focused runtime evidence or a supported static form before they become canonical relationships. Do not infer provider or model behavior from an identifier alone.
